invariant: INV-50
file: sha512.c
catches: sha2_equiv_test
reason: a host object's finalize takes a second block for the length when
  the 1 bit ends 112 bytes into the pending block, where FIPS 180-4
  §5.1.2 still fits the 16-byte length after it. A message of 111 bytes
  modulo 128 then hashes two blocks of padding where the standard hashes
  one, and its digest is wrong; every other length is right, so the
  short published vectors pass. bin/sha2_equiv_test runs every length
  from 0 to 529 on sha512.c's first arm against the second, and the
  message of 111 bytes differs where the one of 110 agrees.

--- old
    s->block[s->fill++] = 0x80;
    if (s->fill > SHA512_BLOCK - 16) {
        memset(s->block + s->fill, 0, SHA512_BLOCK - s->fill);
--- new
    s->block[s->fill++] = 0x80;
    if (s->fill >= SHA512_BLOCK - 16) {
        memset(s->block + s->fill, 0, SHA512_BLOCK - s->fill);
